    "turn_text": "Welcome to the Witness podcast from the BBC World Service with me, Claire Bose. On the 20th of September, 2001, in an historic speech, President George W. Bush launched a war on terror in response to the 911 attacks. Just a few days earlier, Congress had given him the power to order military action against any person, organisation or country suspected of involvement in the attacks. Only one member of Congress, Barbara Lee, had voted against it.",
