  {
    "episode_id": 76905,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76905.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Some of the speakers, for me, got a bit too political, a bit too out of context of the memorial service. And it became too much of a political service in many ways. But the member of the clergy, his name was Nathan Baxter in his sermon, brought it back. It was a very powerful sermon. And I remember in that he said, as we act, let us not become the evil that we deplore. And I wrote that down on the program that I had. And you know, that for me was the final result.",
